    "input_texts": [
      "Title: ServiceNow Filter Panel Field Selection Pitfalls\nDescription: Key observations about field selection, value setting, and condition chaining in the Change Request filter.\n- The filter panel uses a combobox (bid a1181) to select the field for each condition, displaying '-- choose field --' initially.\n- After selecting a field, a separate value chooser combobox (e.g., a1639 for 'Type') appears to set the condition value.\n- Clicking a visible option in the value chooser may fail; using 'select_option' on the combobox bid is a reliable alternative.\n- Each new AND condition is added by clicking a specific button (e.g., a1303, a1781) that updates the button text to reflect the current condition.\n- The 'Model' field supports an 'is empty string' operator (bid a2579) to filter for blank values.\n- The 'Requested by' field requires manual text entry into a textbox (bid a2118) rather than a dropdown selection.\n- The filter logic is cumulative AND, meaning all conditions must be met simultaneously.\n- The field chooser dropdown (e.g., a1659, a2135) remains focused immediately after adding a new condition, ready for input.\n- The workflow stops after setting up the 'Model' condition; 'Short description' and 'State' conditions were not completed in this run."
